# ACL for the rider listener (9001), which runs WITHOUT the go-auth plugin.
#
# Read-only on the public transit tree. Bus positions are not secret — a bus on
# a public road is observable by anyone — so riders need no credential and the
# mobile app ships with no embedded secret to leak.
#
# `topic`, not `pattern`. A pattern rule is for ACLs containing %u (username)
# or %c (client id) substitutions; using it without either makes mosquitto log
# "ACL pattern 'transit/#' does not contain '%c' or '%u'" and is simply the
# wrong directive for a fixed topic.
#
# Rules here that appear before any `user` line apply to anonymous clients.
# There is deliberately no write rule and no rule mentioning driver/#, so an
# anonymous client can neither publish nor read driver topics: anything not
# granted here is denied, and this listener has no plugin to defer to.
#
# Drivers and the backend do not use this file at all. They connect on
# listeners that load the plugin, which resolves their permissions against the
# API instead.

topic read transit/#
